{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520479-creating-tradition-equivalent-hit-marks-using-sorcerers","id":1520479,"title":"Creating Tradition equivalent HIT Marks using sorcerers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-12T16:29:51-07:00","id":1520479,"title":"Creating Tradition equivalent HIT Marks using sorcerers?","content":"I was thinking that perhaps the Traditions can utilize sorcerer societies such as the Ancient Order of the Aeon Rites to help in the creation of their own shock troops. This can be done through the use of sorcery paths like Summoning, Warding and Binding (which are all a part of one path), Alchemy, Cursing/Path of Fortune, Enchantment, and the static shaman paths.<br /> <br /> However, there is the issue of experienced sorcerers being needed for stronger shock troops. Fortunately, using awakened mind magic, I believe it is possible to quickly and easily turn even a novice sorcerer into a master. It might even be a good idea to create their own sorcerer society, completely funded and controlled by Tradition masters, and use them in a similar manner to how vampires use revenants. Maybe combine a few sorcerers with different paths to create a powerful one.<br /> <br /> That's just what I think, what would you do?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T17:25:50-07:00","id":1520486,"title":"","content":"The Traditions have plenty of sorcerers of their own. A typical mage was recruited by a Tradition as a Sleeper with potential. After which teaching them sorcery is the way to instruct them in a Tradition's paradigm, hoping that it'll trigger an Awakening. Unfortunately they're no good as shock troops cause it takes a lot and time and effort to teach sorcery, you'd never be able to do it en masse. But It's not like the Technocracy is creating HIT Marks en masse either. The only difference is that in their creation the Technocrats are willing to cut moral corners a Tradition mage generally won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T18:22:35-07:00","id":1520493,"title":"","content":"I would have figured that the Tradition equivalent to HITMarks would be golems, homunculi, and whatever weird things Etherites build in their labs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T18:42:24-07:00","id":1520494,"title":"","content":"Tradition Cyborgs would be subtler too. Well crafted artificial eyes or artificial ears that make chocliar implants look primitive and. Simple wiring that reconnects severed spinal cords. Restoring normalcy would be the more likely goal. Although some subtle perks could be woven in.<br /> <br /> Tradition Cyborgs would be designed to be more coincidental. But certain impressive advantages could go unnoticed. And unnoticed magicks are coincidental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T21:53:18-07:00","id":1520499,"title":"","content":"These are great responses, the main reason I though of outsourcing work to sorcerers was because I heard golem and whatever else the traditions had were prone to paradox, and that they didn't have the same materials or expertise to build their own HIT Marks.<br /> <br /> I also felt that if the technocrats retaliated or decided to attack the traditions for whatever reason, sorcerers could be used to take the brunt of the attack, or even be used to act as bait. <br /> <br /> It would be great to see the traditions use constructs more often against the technocrats if it really isnt harmful for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}